flowchart TD
    Client[Client]
    Start[HTTP request]
    Client --> Start
    Start --> Route{Request route and credentials}

    subgraph Session[Session login and cookie plus CSRF path]
        CsrfGet[GET /api/auth/csrf]
        CsrfToken[Return token; set XSRF-TOKEN cookie]
        LoginPost[POST /api/auth/login with email/password and X-CSRF-TOKEN]
        AuthManager[AuthenticationManager authenticates credentials]
        CreateSession[AuthController stores SecurityContext in HttpSession; rotates existing session ID]
        SessionCookie[Response sets JSESSIONID session cookie]
        SessionRequest[Subsequent /api request with JSESSIONID]
        CsrfCheck[CSRF filter checks unsafe methods using XSRF-TOKEN cookie and X-CSRF-TOKEN header]
        SessionAuth[Session SecurityContext -> RelayUserPrincipal]
        MemberCheck[RecordService -> ProjectAccessService.requireMember(projectId, userId)]
        RoleDecision{Member role?}
        ManagerCheck[Manager-only operations: requireManager accepts OWNER or ADMIN]
        SessionAllowed[Continue to controller/service]
        SessionDenied[Non-member: project not found; MEMBER on manager-only action: 403]
        CsrfGet --> CsrfToken --> LoginPost --> AuthManager --> CreateSession --> SessionCookie --> SessionRequest --> CsrfCheck --> SessionAuth --> MemberCheck --> RoleDecision
        RoleDecision -->|OWNER / ADMIN / MEMBER| SessionAllowed
        RoleDecision -->|No membership| SessionDenied
        SessionAllowed -. manager-only operation .-> ManagerCheck
        ManagerCheck -->|OWNER or ADMIN| SessionAllowed
        ManagerCheck -->|MEMBER| SessionDenied
    end

    subgraph ApiKey[API-key filter path]
        Bearer[Authorization: Bearer relay_*]
        Matcher[ApiKeyRequestMatcher recognizes /api/v1 generated routes and dynamic record routes]
        Filter[ApiKeyAuthenticationFilter runs before UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter]
        Verify[ApiKeyService authenticates token; usage limit check]
        Principal[Set SecurityContext principal ApiKeyPrincipal; authority API_KEY]
        ApiRoute{Generated /api/v1 route?}
        Authority[Security rule requires API_KEY]
        KeyScope[RecordService checks requested project and environment match key projectId/environmentId]
        KeyAllowed[Continue as key-scoped project/environment]
        Invalid[Invalid/unavailable key: 401; usage rejection returns its API error]
        KeyCsrf[CSRF skipped for generated API routes and matching bearer-token record routes]
        Bearer --> Matcher --> Filter --> Verify
        Verify -->|invalid| Invalid
        Verify -->|valid| Principal --> KeyCsrf --> ApiRoute
        ApiRoute -->|Yes| Authority --> KeyAllowed
        ApiRoute -->|Dynamic record route| KeyScope --> KeyAllowed
    end

    Route -->|Browser session auth / ordinary /api endpoints| CsrfGet
    Route -->|Matching API route with Bearer token| Bearer
    Route -->|Missing or invalid Bearer token on generated route| Filter

    Note[Important: API-key requests do not look up project_members roles. They are restricted by key project/environment scope; project-member role checks apply to session-authenticated requests.]
    KeyScope -. authorization distinction .-> Note
    MemberCheck -. authorization distinction .-> Note

    classDef success fill:#e7f5e8,stroke:#39844a,color:#152b18;
    classDef failure fill:#fdeaea,stroke:#b64242,color:#341515;
    class SessionAllowed,KeyAllowed success;
    class SessionDenied,Invalid failure;
